# AnkiWeb LITE

Read `docs/ankiweb-lite-playbook.md` before building or proposing a shared deck.

**Lock (2026-10-04):** Wave 1 = PTCB 40 · Series 63 40 · CFA L1 40. Refresh existing CFA L2 LITE (50) listing; do not upload a second L2. Skip language/civic LITEs (0–3 downloads measured).

Default size **40** unique FULL GUIDs, blueprint-weighted, human-read. **AnkiWeb samples random notes from the whole deck — every LITE card must be sample-grade.** Title starts with a **searchable token** (`PTCB`, `PTCE`, `CFA`, `NASAA`). AnkiWeb search is one token; `63` does not match. **Do not put `LITE` in the public AnkiWeb title** (hurts conversion; set 2026-10-21) — say “sample” only in the description.

Do not pick “first N of the CSV.” Do not LITE a FULL that failed the card standard.

## Share (agent — do not ask the user)

AnkiConnect has **no** share API. After import + `sync`, the agent shares via Cursor browser:

1. `deckNamesAndIds` → id of the titled LITE deck (no `LITE` in name)
2. Open `https://ankiweb.net/decks/share/{deckId}` (logged-in AnkiWeb session)
3. Fill Title / Tags / Support / Description from `listing.txt`; check ownership box; click Share
4. Capture Shared ID from `/shared/info/{id}`; write `docs/ankiweb-lite-ledger.md`

Full steps: playbook § **Share procedure**. Never stop at “right-click Share in Anki” while Connect + browser login are available.
